// Title: WhoAmI as Parameter
// Sigma ID: e9142d84-fbe0-401d-ac50-3e519fb00c89
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-11-29 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1033
// Tags: car.2016-03-001
// Description: Detects a suspicious process command line that uses whoami as first parameter (as e.g. used by
//   EfsPotato)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/blackarrowsec/status/1463805700602224645?s=12
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_whoami_as_param.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe whoami"
